From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] deviceManager: support sinks that PulseAudio already owns

Two things stop audiod ever finding a device on a Halium port, and between
them nothing is ever routed: audiod reports no internal device, so
module-palm-policy is never given an output device, never moves a stream off
the virtual null sinks, and every sound is played into the bin with a
perfectly healthy audio stack underneath.

First, the config is looked up by the card id PDM reports, and PDM does not
report one on every platform - on a Pixel 3a it arrives empty while the card
is described by name ("sdm670-intcodec-s4-snd-card"). No entry can match an
empty key whatever the config says, so fall back to matching the card name.

Second, a device could only be brought up by asking PulseAudio to load an
ALSA sink for it. That is wrong wherever something else already owns the
card: on Halium that is module-droid-card, and the Android HAL has to keep
it, because the HAL is what sets up the mixer paths - talking to the PCM
directly generally gets a device that opens and stays silent. Loading an
ALSA sink there means two things fighting over the same PCM.

Allow a sink to be declared as type "preloaded", meaning it already exists
in PulseAudio and audiod should register it without loading anything. The
check lives in loadInternalCard() rather than at the call site because there
are two paths in: addInternalCard() when the card is discovered, and
eventMixerStatus() replaying registered cards once the mixer is ready. On a
cold boot the mixer is not ready when the card is discovered, so it is the
second path that runs - handling only the first leaves cold boots silent
while a hand-restarted audiod works, which is a thoroughly confusing way for
this to fail.

Announcing the connection is part of the same job. PulseAudio normally
answers a load with a device-connection reply, and that reply is what tells
audioRouter a device exists and makes it route the virtual sinks onto it.
Nothing sends it for a sink we did not load, so raise it here or the device
is registered and never routed to.

A card entry named "*" matches whichever internal card was found, after the id
and the name have both failed. Naming the card is only worth the trouble when a
machine has more than one internal card and the wrong one could win - a codec
plus an HDMI output, say. Where there is one card, or where the sink is owned by
something else and audiod only needs to know its name, the card it is called by
carries no information, and demanding it means no machine makes a sound until
somebody boots it and reads the name back out of the log.

Nothing else needs to change: routing is by sink name the whole way down -
audioRouter passes a name to setSoundOutputOnRange() and module-palm-policy
resolves it with pa_namereg_get() - so a sink of that name is all it needs.

Upstream-Status: Pending [intended for webosose/audiod]
---
--- a/src/modules/deviceManager/deviceManager.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/deviceManager/deviceManager.cpp
@@ -90,6 +90,32 @@
 {
     PM_LOG_INFO(MSGID_DEVICE_MANAGER, INIT_KVCOUNT, "loadInternalCard cardInfo.isConnected = %d",cardInfo.isConnected);
     bool ret = false;
+    if (cardInfo.type == "preloaded")
+    {
+        // The sink already exists in PulseAudio and something else owns the
+        // hardware - module-droid-card on a Halium device, where the Android HAL
+        // has to keep the card because it is what sets up the mixer paths.
+        // Loading an ALSA sink here would fight it for the PCM. Registering is
+        // enough: routing is by sink name, so the router only needs a sink of
+        // this name to exist.
+        //
+        // Nothing else will report it as connected, either. Normally PulseAudio
+        // answers the load with a device-connection reply and that is what tells
+        // audioRouter a device exists and makes it route the virtual sinks onto
+        // it, so announce it here or the device is registered but never routed
+        // to, and every stream stays on the virtual sink it was created on.
+        if (!cardInfo.isConnected)
+        {
+            PM_LOG_INFO(MSGID_DEVICE_MANAGER, INIT_KVCOUNT,\
+                "sink %s is preloaded, registering without loading a card",\
+                cardInfo.name.c_str());
+            cardInfo.isConnected = true;
+            mObjAudioMixer->callBackDeviceConnectionStatus(cardInfo.name,\
+                cardInfo.name, "", utils::eDeviceConnected,\
+                utils::ePulseMixer, cardInfo.isOutput);
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
     if (cardInfo.isConnected == false)
     {
         PM_LOG_DEBUG("calling load internal card with parameters cardno :%d,deviceno:%d,status:%d,isoutput:%d,name:%s",\
@@ -817,6 +843,32 @@
     {
         bool deviceFoundInlist = false;
         it = internalDevices.find(cardId);
+        if (it == internalDevices.end() && !cardName.empty())
+        {
+            // PDM does not report a card id on every platform - it arrives
+            // empty on Halium devices, where the card is described by name
+            // only - so fall back to matching the name before giving up.
+            PM_LOG_INFO(MSGID_DEVICE_MANAGER, INIT_KVCOUNT,\
+                "no config entry for cardId '%s', trying cardName '%s'",\
+                cardId.c_str(), cardName.c_str());
+            it = internalDevices.find(cardName);
+        }
+        if (it == internalDevices.end())
+        {
+            // Last resort: an entry named "*" describes whichever internal card
+            // was found. Naming the card is only worth the trouble when a device
+            // has more than one and the wrong one could win - a machine with a
+            // codec and an HDMI output, say. Where there is one internal card,
+            // or where the sink is owned by something else and audiod only has
+            // to know its name, the card it is called by carries no information
+            // and demanding it means every machine needs a config file written
+            // from a booted device before it makes a sound.
+            it = internalDevices.find("*");
+            if (it != internalDevices.end())
+                PM_LOG_INFO(MSGID_DEVICE_MANAGER, INIT_KVCOUNT,\
+                    "no entry for cardId '%s' or cardName '%s', using the "
+                    "wildcard entry", cardId.c_str(), cardName.c_str());
+        }
         if (it != internalDevices.end())
         {
             for (auto& deviceInfo : it->second)
